n. Render pipeline: layout-driven prompt assembly via anchor-slot fill, dropping `hydrate` and hardcoded section labels
    [ ] 'content/backend/render_pipeline/render_service.py': Replace `hydrate`-based substitution with parse-layout → bucket-resolvers → slot-fill → join
        - `render_prompt`: read layout, call `_parse_layout` to get ordered `list[str]` of anchor names; flatten all resolvers (base + domain + prompt) into one list; bucket into `dict[str, list[Resolver]]` keyed by `.anchor`; for each bucket, call the type-dispatched renderer; build final string by iterating layout anchors in order, emitting `¤¤ {anchor} ¤¤\n{content}` only for anchors that received content; skip anchors with no content
        - add `_parse_layout(raw: str) -> list[str]`: split on `§`, strip whitespace from each token, return ordered list of anchor names
        - add `_flatten_resolvers(cmd) -> list[e.Resolver]`: consolidate base/domain/prompt resolvers per existing `inherit_domain` / `inherit_base` logic into a single flat list
        - add `_render_resolver(resolver) -> str`: match on type, dispatch to existing `_res_*` methods
        - remove the `self.shaper.hydrate(template, repl_map)` call from `render_prompt`
    [ ] 'content/backend/render_pipeline/render_service.py': Change per-type renderers to emit `¤ name ¤` file delimiters only (no section headers, no XML-style tags)
        - `_res_multi_doc`: change `<{name}>\n{content}\n</{name}>` → `¤ {name} ¤\n{content}\n¤ {name} ¤`; join with `"\n\n"`
        - `_res_repo_content`: remove the `"¤¤ Repository Contents ¤¤"` header line; change `¤filepath="{p}"¤` → `¤ {p} ¤` (opening and closing); join with `"\n\n"`
        - `_res_manifest` / `_build_manifest`: change `<{tag}>\n...\n</{tag}>` → `¤¤ {tag} ¤¤\n` + `¤ {p} ¤\n{line_count} lines` entries joined by `"\n\n"`
    [ ] 'content/backend/render_pipeline/content_shaper.py': Remove `hydrate` method (or leave unused); keep `apply_truncation`
        - `SystemKeys.DELIM` and the regex-based substitution in `hydrate` are no longer needed by the render pipeline
        - prohibition: do not remove `apply_truncation` — it is still used by `_res_multi_doc`
    [ ] 'content/a_lib/templates/prompt.layout': Rewrite to contain only `§anchor§` declaration lines, one per line, in display order
        - example: `§base_fragments§`, `§repo_content§`, `§domain_fragments§`, `§prompt_fragments§` (actual anchors depend on config)
        - prohibition: no `¤¤` section labels, no free text, no comments in the layout file — it is consumed by `_parse_layout` which only recognises `§...§`
    [ ] 'content/.clanker/config.yaml' (and/or shared config): Ensure every anchor declared in `prompt.layout` has a corresponding resolver entry with matching `anchor` value
        - existing anchors (`repo_content`, `domain_fragments`, `prompt_fragments`) are already present in domain/prompt resolver lists
        - if a new anchor (e.g. `base_fragments`) is added to the layout, a matching resolver entry must exist in the config or the section will silently not render
        - prohibition: do not add anchors to the layout that have no resolver — they will be dropped at render time, which is correct behaviour, but a dangling anchor in layout with no config entry suggests a bug
```
Backlog tail, Selected item/items:
9. Rework prompt rendering
    - The prompt layout file declares sections via `§section_name§` markers. Each marker is both the section header in the output and the key that resolvers attach to via their `anchor` field.

    - `PromptServiceImpl.render_prompt` — replace the flat `hydrate` call with the following assembly:

    a. Fetch the layout from `self.files.read_asset(e.ClankerAssets.layouts.PROMPT)`. Parse it into an ordered list of section names by extracting all `§...§` matches in order of appearance. Build `sections: dict[str, list[e.Resolver]]` initialized with each section name as a key mapped to an empty list.

    b. Collect resolvers (same as current `_get_repl_map` logic, but return the flat `list[e.Resolver]` instead of a resolved dict):
        - Normal: extend with `cmd.domain.resolvers` if `cmd.prompt.render.inherit_domain`, then extend with `cmd.prompt.render.resolvers`.
        - Hot: collect `MultiDocResolver` instances from domain + prompt resolvers, extract `.mode_instruction` / `.output_instruction` / `.history` files, build a `lone_resolver`, append it.

    c. Derive the global type order: `order = sorted({type(r) for r in resolvers})` (alphabetical by class name).

    d. For each `res` in `resolvers`:
        - If `res.anchor not in sections`: raise (or `ec.accept` a soft complaint and skip — pick one, document it).
        - `sections[res.anchor].append(res)`.

    e. Evict empty sections: `sections = {k: v for k, v in sections.items() if v}`.

    f. Sort each section's list so that the order of resolvers within a section matches `order` (by type name).

    g. `render = ""`.

    h. For each `(section_name, res_list)` in `sections.items()`:
        - `render += f"¤¤ {section_name} ¤¤\n"`
        - For each `res` in `res_list`:
            - Dispatch: `content = self._res_multi_doc(res)[res.anchor]` if `isinstance(res, e.MultiDocResolver)`, else `self._res_repo_content(res)[res.anchor]` if `isinstance(res, e.RepoContentResolver)`, else `self._res_manifest(res)[res.anchor]`.
            - `render += content`
        - `render += "\n"`

    i. `render` is the final prompt text. Return it in `PromptRenderResult` as before (lines = `len(render.splitlines())`, chars = `len(render)`).

    - `_res_multi_doc`, `_res_repo_content`, `_res_manifest` are unchanged. They still return `dict[str, str]`; the caller just indexes `[res.anchor]`.

    - `PromptContentShaper.hydrate` is no longer called from the main path. It can remain for any future inline substitution need, or be removed if nothing else uses it. `apply_truncation` stays as-is (called inside `_res_multi_doc`).

    - Hot prompt path: same as above, except step (b) produces the `lone_resolver`. Steps (c)–(i) are identical. The `prompt_mode` field in `PromptRenderResult` already distinguishes `RenderNormalPromptCmd` vs `RenderHotPromptCmd` — no change needed there.

    - Files touched: `content/backend/render_pipeline/render_service.py` (method `render_prompt`, remove or repurpose `_get_repl_map`). No changes to entities, keyboard, ingestion, controller, or the shaper's truncation logic.
Backlog tail end

